<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a conveyor pusher?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A conveyor pusher pushes product off the side of a conveyor using a pneumatic cylinder or servo actuator. Pushers fire when a sensor detects product in position and a PLC triggers the push. Used for lane diverting, <a href="/conveyor-functions/reject-systems/">reject systems</a>, and product routing.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is a blade diverter?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A blade diverter uses a pivoting arm that swings into the product path at a 30 or 45 degree angle, deflecting product onto a spur conveyor. Blades handle cases, totes, and cartons at speeds up to 300+ FPM. Gentler than pushers because they redirect product momentum rather than applying lateral force.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">Pusher vs. diverter, what is the difference?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A pusher applies lateral force perpendicular to the belt, fast but impactful. A diverter redirects product at an angle using existing forward momentum, gentler but requires more conveyor length. Use pushers for lightweight items and rejects. Use diverters for heavy products and gentle routing to multiple spur lines.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How fast can pushers and diverters operate?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Pneumatic pushers: 50-200ms. Servo pushers: 30-100ms. Blade diverters: 100-500ms. ARB and sliding shoe sorters operate continuously with no cycle time limitation. The mechanism must complete its cycle before the next product arrives, at 200 FPM with 12-inch spacing, each product arrives every 300ms.</p>

</div>
